// Journal features: authors with details, classification, numbering by
// section, an appendix, citations and a BibTeX bibliography.
title "Gaps Between Sums of Two Squares"
author "Ada Lovelace", affiliation: "University of London, UK", email: "ada@example.org", orcid: "0000-0002-1825-0097"
author "Charles Babbage", affiliation: "Cambridge", url: "https://example.org/cb"
author "Mary Somerville and John Herschel"
msc "11N36 (primary); 11E25 (secondary)"
keywords "sums of two squares, short intervals"
numbering by section
bibliography "journal.bib"

abstract
  We improve the exponent $1/2$ of [@hooley, Thm. 2; @landau].

section Introduction #intro

Landau [@landau] proved

    B(x) ~ K x/sqrt(log x)   #asym

By Theorem @main and Lemmas @a and @b, see (@asym) and Section @intro;
also [@vallee; @erdos; @thesis; @arxiv; @parens; @dblp; @biblatex] and [@arxiv, §2].
The paper @hooley and the formula (@asym) are different things.

theorem "Main" #main
  Every interval $[x, x + x^(1/4 + epsilon)]$ contains one.

lemma #a
  First.

lemma #b
  Second, by [@landau, p. $305$].

appendix

section Computations #comp

lemma #c
  As in Appendix @comp, Lemma @c holds:

      g(x) <= 2 x^(1/4)   #bound
